1
00:00:08,380 --> 00:00:09,210
YAMU!

2
00:00:09,293 --> 00:00:11,757
YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!

3
00:00:11,840 --> 00:00:12,740
YAMU!

4
00:00:30,460 --> 00:00:31,460
You're on a move!

5
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:18,500
To the palace!

6
00:01:25,440 --> 00:01:27,180
Who dares trespass?

7
00:01:27,340 --> 00:01:28,977
Halt in the name of the pharaoh!

8
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:30,360
You fools!

9
00:01:30,660 --> 00:01:32,720
Step aside if you value your souls!

10
00:01:33,060 --> 00:01:34,400
Stand tall, men!

11
00:01:39,080 --> 00:01:40,340
Sound the alarm!

12
00:01:44,140 --> 00:01:45,757
Mahan, is something the matter?

13
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:47,016
The Millennium Ring.

14
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:50,120
We are in the presence
of pure evil. Oh no!

15
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:56,000
Who goes there?

16
00:01:57,040 --> 00:02:02,040
Pardon the interruption, but apparently
someone left me off the guest list. Bakura!

17
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:06,400
What do you want from me?

18
00:02:07,260 --> 00:02:10,907
Now, is that any way to speak
to an old friend, your highness?

19
00:02:11,220 --> 00:02:13,985
I believe you know what
I came here to acquire.

20
00:02:14,140 --> 00:02:15,600
The Millennium Items.

21
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:19,899
So you have been paying attention
to me all these years, haven't you?

22
00:02:27,260 --> 00:02:30,097
All right, let me see if I've
got this straight, shoddy.

23
00:02:30,180 --> 00:02:32,057
The only way to get to the Pharaoh is to

24
00:02:32,140 --> 00:02:34,728
find a doorway inside
the Millennium Puzzle?

25
00:02:35,020 --> 00:02:37,660
Yes, but the puzzle
contains many doorways,

26
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:40,417
some of which lead to
dark and dangerous realms.

27
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:42,857
Therefore, I will guide
you through this journey.

28
00:02:42,940 --> 00:02:46,411
But when you wish to return,
I'm afraid you're on your own.

29
00:02:46,880 --> 00:02:48,200
We got no choice.

30
00:02:48,460 --> 00:02:49,677
Now let's do this, Yug!

31
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:51,560
All for one and one for all.

32
00:02:51,900 --> 00:02:52,880
Thanks a lot.

33
00:02:53,160 --> 00:02:54,917
Really, but I'm doing this alone.

34
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:55,980
Are you nuts?

35
00:02:56,540 --> 00:03:00,660
Look, guys, I've put all your lives
in danger enough times already.

36
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:03,417
This is something that I
need to do for the Pharaoh,

37
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:05,277
and I'm going to do it on my own.

38
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:08,737
You should realize by now that
it can't ditch us that easily.

39
00:03:08,820 --> 00:03:12,585
We've stuck with you on every
adventure for the last four years.

40
00:03:12,680 --> 00:03:15,520
You think we're gonna
stop now? Are you sure?

41
00:03:16,680 --> 00:03:18,837
Everyone, hold hands and concentrate.

42
00:03:18,920 --> 00:03:20,400
We must pool our energy.

43
00:03:27,940 --> 00:03:31,780
Pharaoh, wherever you are, I will find you

44
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:34,950
Now,

45
00:03:35,060 --> 00:03:36,397
in the name of the great pharaoh,

46
00:03:36,480 --> 00:03:39,774
I shall invoke the sacred
energies of the Millennium Key

47
00:03:41,060 --> 00:03:45,119
Please guide us through the mystic
labyrinth of the Millennium Puzzle

48
00:03:51,320 --> 00:03:56,320
I hope I didn't ruin your
little celebration, gentlemen.

49
00:03:56,640 --> 00:03:58,617
Your mockery is a disgrace to the pharaoh,

50
00:03:58,700 --> 00:04:00,757
and for that you shall be punished, rogue.

51
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:01,940
Not so fast.

52
00:04:02,180 --> 00:04:07,004
I reside in the outskirts of your little
kingdom, so your rules don't apply to me.

53
00:04:07,240 --> 00:04:11,180
Now, if you wouldn't mind, hand
over your millennium items. What?

54
00:04:11,760 --> 00:04:13,120
I didn't mean for free.

55
00:04:13,320 --> 00:04:14,760
I come bearing gifts.

56
00:04:15,480 --> 00:04:17,080
You stole those!

57
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:18,340
How dare you!

58
00:04:18,480 --> 00:04:20,557
I assumed these trinkets
wouldn't be enough,

59
00:04:20,640 --> 00:04:23,120
so I brought another token of my esteem.

60
00:04:26,300 --> 00:04:27,800
What is going on?

61
00:04:31,440 --> 00:04:33,820
Say hello to your previous king!

62
00:04:34,460 --> 00:04:37,840
You dare disrespect the
tomb of a former pharaoh?

63
00:04:38,380 --> 00:04:40,460
Now you've taken this too far!

64
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:44,540
The Korra, your soul must be
judged by the Millennium Items!

65
00:04:45,340 --> 00:04:46,300
He's right!

66
00:04:46,520 --> 00:04:48,991
Guards, bring us a sealing tablet at once!

67
00:04:49,180 --> 00:04:51,260
Let the Millennium Trial begin!

68
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:55,460
Your weak magic will never contain me!

69
00:04:57,060 --> 00:05:00,540
No mortal can resist the
power of the sacred items!

70
00:05:00,920 --> 00:05:02,820
Hold on! What is it?

71
00:05:03,080 --> 00:05:05,960
The Millennium Scale is
unable to find balance!

72
00:05:06,280 --> 00:05:09,162
That means the evil in
his heart is immeasurable!

73
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:13,060
Yes, I see a darkness
that knows no bounds.

74
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:17,760
His soul is a bottomless pit in
which thrives a terrifying creature.

75
00:05:18,880 --> 00:05:23,140
Now, Millennium Key, reveal
the beast that lurks within.

76
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:38,840
That's no ordinary beast.

77
00:05:38,980 --> 00:05:40,540
What did you see, Shaddaa?

78
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:43,228
The most powerful being
I've ever witnessed.

79
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:46,580
That ceiling tablet is
far too small! Ridiculous!

80
00:05:46,900 --> 00:05:47,800
Seto is right.

81
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:50,235
We've never had any difficulty before.

82
00:05:59,500 --> 00:06:00,330
Unbelievable!

83
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:04,331
How can such a creature live
in the heart of a petty thief?

84
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:08,377
Let me introduce my friend.

85
00:06:08,460 --> 00:06:13,840
Diabound, meet the pharaoh, and pharaoh,
meet the instrument of your demise.

86
00:06:14,220 --> 00:06:16,177
I am afraid you are mistaken, thief.

87
00:06:16,260 --> 00:06:18,025
Your monster's fate is sealed.

88
00:06:18,640 --> 00:06:20,580
Millennium Rod, activate!

89
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:32,120
Just as I suspected, his
soul has been cleansed.

90
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:33,753
Thank you, Master Seto.

91
00:06:33,900 --> 00:06:35,340
You saved my life.

92
00:06:35,660 --> 00:06:38,377
That horrible creature
was controlling my mind.

93
00:06:38,460 --> 00:06:40,300
And now I'm finally free.

94
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:45,040
Free to annihilate you, that
is. Impossible. It didn't work.

95
00:06:46,380 --> 00:06:48,300
This doesn't make any sense.

96
00:06:58,720 --> 00:07:02,940
It looks as if I've already won
this game before it's even begun.

97
00:07:04,500 --> 00:07:06,620
Yugi, come on. Wake up, pal.

98
00:07:11,860 --> 00:07:13,060
You okay, Joey?

99
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:14,950
All right.

100
00:07:15,140 --> 00:07:16,552
Rise and shine, you two.

101
00:07:18,940 --> 00:07:19,980
Where are we?

102
00:07:20,260 --> 00:07:22,907
We're inside the Millennium
Puzzle, remember?

103
00:07:23,280 --> 00:07:25,580
This place seems bigger than last time.

104
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:27,588
Did you do some remodeling?

105
00:07:28,100 --> 00:07:32,218
The puzzle is a reflection of the
Pharaoh's mind and is ever-changing.

106
00:07:32,440 --> 00:07:33,360
No wonder.

107
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:36,417
Yeah, I guess that explains why
this place is so complicated.

108
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:38,257
Well, what are we waiting for?

109
00:07:38,340 --> 00:07:40,340
Let's get up and find the Pharaoh!

110
00:07:41,940 --> 00:07:43,460
Alright, shoddy old pal!

111
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:47,237
Use that Millennium thingy of yours
and point us in the right direction!

112
00:07:47,320 --> 00:07:48,760
It's a Millennium King!

113
00:07:51,980 --> 00:07:55,420
Are you telling me Yugi
left the country? Yes, sir!

114
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:57,617
Our flight logs indicate
that he boarded a jet

115
00:07:57,700 --> 00:08:00,818
bound for Cairo with three
companions just yesterday!

116
00:08:01,240 --> 00:08:03,475
Why would the Geek Squad fly to Egypt?

117
00:08:03,660 --> 00:08:04,620
And why now?

118
00:08:07,780 --> 00:08:09,640
Why don't you hold on to this?

119
00:08:12,100 --> 00:08:12,997
Hold on.

120
00:08:13,080 --> 00:08:15,940
Didn't this belong to Pegasus? Why, yes.

121
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:18,840
And it holds many answers about your past.

122
00:08:19,100 --> 00:08:21,806
Bring it to Egypt, and
I'll tell you the rest.

123
00:08:22,500 --> 00:08:24,940
But Korra must have gotten to Yugi also.

124
00:08:28,820 --> 00:08:33,177
I told you you'd be powerless against
the dark energy of my dear Bound!

125
00:08:33,260 --> 00:08:38,320
Sacred Guardians of the Pharaoh, we must
unite to conquer this adversary. Yes.

126
00:08:43,060 --> 00:08:45,413
You mean to tell me you have dual discs?

127
00:08:45,580 --> 00:08:47,000
What is a dual disc?

128
00:08:47,900 --> 00:08:48,730
Oh,

129
00:08:48,813 --> 00:08:50,437
that's a device used
for calling forth shadow

130
00:08:50,520 --> 00:08:53,597
creatures that have been
sealed away in stone tablets.

131
00:08:53,680 --> 00:08:55,777
Once these monsters have
been trapped in stone,

132
00:08:55,860 --> 00:08:58,617
they're stored in tablet
sanctuaries until someone

133
00:08:58,700 --> 00:09:01,857
summons them using a
mechanism called a dia-dianc.

134
00:09:01,940 --> 00:09:03,540
Like ancient dual discs.

135
00:09:03,860 --> 00:09:07,680
Well, can the Guardians
come out and play? Careful.

136
00:09:08,040 --> 00:09:09,200
He's a strong one.

137
00:09:09,480 --> 00:09:12,200
We must combine our powers. Fear not.

138
00:09:12,380 --> 00:09:15,200
I can defeat this thief on my own. Seto!

139
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:18,148
Now, creature of darkness,
I call upon thee.

140
00:09:18,520 --> 00:09:21,520
Awaken from thy slumber
and join me in this battle.

141
00:09:33,720 --> 00:09:35,800
So this is how it all began.

142
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:38,820
And now I summon Goreskoloth!

143
00:09:44,340 --> 00:09:46,800
Now this is a shadow game.

144
00:09:47,640 --> 00:09:51,000
Goreskoloth, it's time to
wage war with Izdiabound!

145
00:09:52,560 --> 00:09:55,480
I'm witnessing the
origin of Duel Monsters!

146
00:10:00,580 --> 00:10:04,777
No one who disrespects the
pharaohs shall go unpunished I

147
00:10:04,860 --> 00:10:08,272
must be watching one of the
first shadow games ever played

148
00:10:09,040 --> 00:10:10,240
Goresgoloth, attack!

149
00:10:10,580 --> 00:10:12,200
Vanquish his Diabound!

150
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:19,500
Now, Wing Sage Valgos, come forth!

151
00:10:20,560 --> 00:10:21,390
What?

152
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:23,520
He summoned another creature?

153
00:10:30,940 --> 00:10:32,760
Oh, this can't be.

154
00:10:32,980 --> 00:10:35,451
Only those in the royal court can do that.

155
00:10:35,820 --> 00:10:37,879
Yes, how did you summon that beast?

156
00:10:38,140 --> 00:10:40,320
You do not possess a Diadiank.

157
00:10:43,360 --> 00:10:44,478
Don't you remember?

158
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:47,097
I paid a visit to your old pharaoh's tomb.

159
00:10:47,180 --> 00:10:49,320
And while I was paying my respects,

160
00:10:49,640 --> 00:10:53,620
I thought I might borrow a few
of his little toys like this.

161
00:10:59,160 --> 00:11:03,217
Can't you see that you are interfering
with forces beyond your control?

162
00:11:03,300 --> 00:11:04,380
Obviously not.

163
00:11:04,660 --> 00:11:07,057
I'm in complete control of these forces,

164
00:11:07,140 --> 00:11:11,081
thanks to your former king and his
personal collection of monsters.

165
00:11:11,860 --> 00:11:16,700
You dare disturb the great protectors of
the sacred crypt of King Aknam Cannon?

166
00:11:16,980 --> 00:11:20,697
Those creatures were placed there to
safeguard the tomb of a great pharaoh.

167
00:11:20,780 --> 00:11:22,140
So you say.

168
00:11:22,440 --> 00:11:23,760
But I disagree.

169
00:11:24,200 --> 00:11:25,480
He was a tyrant.

170
00:11:25,760 --> 00:11:29,037
He destroyed my village when
he tried to fashion the Seven

171
00:11:29,120 --> 00:11:32,826
Millennium Items in a selfish
attempt to further his own power.

172
00:11:33,700 --> 00:11:37,524
So it was the previous pharaoh
that created the Millennium Items?

173
00:11:38,500 --> 00:11:39,540
You lie!

174
00:11:39,880 --> 00:11:43,597
King Aknam Cannon put an end to the
great wars that ravaged our nation.

175
00:11:43,680 --> 00:11:45,497
He brought peace and prosperity.

176
00:11:45,580 --> 00:11:48,097
He then created the
Seven Millennium Items to

177
00:11:48,180 --> 00:11:50,697
ensure that harmony would
reign forever in Egypt.

178
00:11:50,780 --> 00:11:51,610
Correct.

179
00:11:51,760 --> 00:11:53,660
Then he gave those tools to us,

180
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:57,497
in order to keep the peace and
help rule the land with justice.

181
00:11:57,580 --> 00:12:01,560
As well as to thwart evildoers
not unlike yourself, Bakura.

182
00:12:02,540 --> 00:12:03,370
Evildoers?

183
00:12:04,760 --> 00:12:06,340
What do you think you are?

184
00:12:06,940 --> 00:12:11,217
The items were built to react with the inner
darkness of the person that holds them.

185
00:12:11,300 --> 00:12:13,677
So the fact that the
seven of you wield these

186
00:12:13,760 --> 00:12:16,557
items makes each and every
one of you an evildoer,

187
00:12:16,640 --> 00:12:20,346
just like your so-called Keeper
of the Peace, King Aknam Cannon.

188
00:12:20,780 --> 00:12:22,320
Your king wanted power.

189
00:12:22,740 --> 00:12:27,337
That's why he devised a plan to use the
seven items to control the entire world.

190
00:12:27,420 --> 00:12:30,067
The secret lies in the
village of Kall 'Elna.

191
00:12:30,180 --> 00:12:31,100
Enough lies.

192
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:33,080
What you speak is treason.

193
00:12:33,840 --> 00:12:37,017
But how can he possibly know
of the village of Kall 'Elna?

194
00:12:37,100 --> 00:12:40,140
The secret of its existence
was buried ages ago.

195
00:12:42,340 --> 00:12:44,937
Hidden deep beneath
the sands of Kall 'Elna

196
00:12:45,020 --> 00:12:47,960
lies a structure known
as the Millennium Stone.

197
00:12:48,640 --> 00:12:52,760
Place the seven items in this stone,
and ultimate power will be yours.

198
00:12:53,040 --> 00:12:54,452
Does he speak the truth?

199
00:12:54,580 --> 00:12:57,340
I don't know where you came from, Bakura.

200
00:12:57,600 --> 00:12:59,697
However, I do know where you must go.

201
00:12:59,780 --> 00:13:01,220
Seto, destroy him!

202
00:13:01,380 --> 00:13:04,968
There is nothing that would
please me more, Master Ak 'Nadin.

203
00:13:05,140 --> 00:13:08,137
Let our shadow game continue as you wish.

204
00:13:08,220 --> 00:13:11,077
But it won't be much of a battle
unless you summon something.

205
00:13:11,160 --> 00:13:15,400
I call upon Battle Ox, Bostet, Spiria,

206
00:13:15,740 --> 00:13:18,640
Zalua, Cards, Illusion Magician.

207
00:13:31,780 --> 00:13:33,620
Now, Magician, attack!

208
00:13:38,620 --> 00:13:40,820
You'll have to do better than that!

209
00:13:41,360 --> 00:13:44,478
Dearbound, teach these
amateurs how to really attack!

210
00:13:45,280 --> 00:13:47,380
Engage with Helical Shockwave!

211
00:13:53,160 --> 00:13:55,000
I've never seen such strength!

212
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:57,000
Yes, but he's outnumbered!

213
00:13:57,200 --> 00:13:59,340
Please, allow me to attack again!

214
00:13:59,500 --> 00:14:02,437
No, Mahad, your creature
would only be destroyed!

215
00:14:02,520 --> 00:14:03,640
Let me try.

216
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:07,597
You will have another chance, but
we need to weaken his monster first.

217
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:09,580
I summon Mystic Horsemen!

218
00:14:15,860 --> 00:14:17,540
Take over, Karim.

219
00:14:17,780 --> 00:14:19,997
With the vast power of
the Millennium Scale,

220
00:14:20,080 --> 00:14:24,940
I invoke the spirits of Battle Ox and
Mystic Horsemen combined together!

221
00:14:26,840 --> 00:14:30,280
This must be the origin of Monster Fusion!

222
00:14:31,080 --> 00:14:33,240
Behold, rabid horsemen!

223
00:14:38,700 --> 00:14:42,120
Now attack is diabound
with battle axe swipe!

224
00:14:45,760 --> 00:14:47,400
Diabound, counterattack!

225
00:14:55,620 --> 00:14:58,017
Looks like your pony's all tied up!

226
00:14:58,100 --> 00:15:01,160
I am afraid that won't last long. What?

227
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:03,660
Mahad, this is your chance.

228
00:15:03,880 --> 00:15:05,998
Then illusion magician, come hither.

229
00:15:06,340 --> 00:15:08,693
Activate your power of binding illusion.

230
00:15:15,340 --> 00:15:18,600
It appears your monster is in a bind now.

231
00:15:19,080 --> 00:15:20,380
Oh, is that so?

232
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:23,060
Diabal, helical shockwave!

233
00:15:32,440 --> 00:15:34,340
How can this possibly be?

234
00:15:34,560 --> 00:15:36,900
One man overpowering six guardians?

235
00:15:39,020 --> 00:15:42,700
If I were you, Pharaoh, I would
consider replacing your staff.

236
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:44,140
That is enough.

237
00:15:44,740 --> 00:15:45,570
Bakura!

238
00:15:45,653 --> 00:15:49,080
You're on sacred ground and
your disrespect is appalling.

239
00:15:49,460 --> 00:15:52,284
It seems I've gotten a
rise out of his highness.

240
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:56,757
Please excuse me for not respecting
a kingdom that destroyed my home.

241
00:15:56,840 --> 00:15:58,160
Deerbound, attack!

242
00:16:00,860 --> 00:16:02,820
Spiria shield, activate!

243
00:16:12,900 --> 00:16:13,730
Isis!

244
00:16:14,560 --> 00:16:16,240
This is not over.

245
00:16:16,380 --> 00:16:17,860
It will be soon enough.

246
00:16:18,280 --> 00:16:22,640
One more attack by my Deerbound and
this palace will be reduced to rubble!

247
00:16:27,380 --> 00:16:30,320
Leave this palace before I remove you!

248
00:16:30,480 --> 00:16:33,774
Farrow, please allow us to
battle this intruder for you!

249
00:16:34,060 --> 00:16:37,280
Bakura, is this the ultimate
shadow game you spoke of?

250
00:16:37,680 --> 00:16:41,917
Trespassing on sacred ground and
tarnishing the very name of my ancestors?

251
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:45,765
You've always been despicable,
but now you've reached a new low!

252
00:16:45,920 --> 00:16:49,567
Please, Farrow, all of a sudden
you care about your ancestors?

253
00:16:49,760 --> 00:16:52,819
Admit it, you don't know
the first thing about them.

254
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:55,760
But here, maybe this will jog your memory!

255
00:16:57,060 --> 00:16:57,890
Oh,

256
00:16:58,080 --> 00:16:59,160
King Aknam Cannon,

257
00:16:59,320 --> 00:17:03,261
I never imagined your return to
the palace would be so disgraceful.

258
00:17:03,420 --> 00:17:05,714
I'm sorry you had to say this, Pharaoh,

259
00:17:05,820 --> 00:17:08,937
but we cannot let this
monster continue to dishonor

260
00:17:09,020 --> 00:17:12,079
our heritage by spouting
false accusations and lies.

261
00:17:12,220 --> 00:17:16,657
And you mustn't believe anything he says
about our former Pharaoh, King Aknam Cannon.

262
00:17:16,740 --> 00:17:18,900
He was kind and just.

263
00:17:19,520 --> 00:17:22,000
Please trust me, I do.

264
00:17:25,260 --> 00:17:28,340
Justice lies with the Egyptian gods.

265
00:17:29,120 --> 00:17:30,660
The Egyptian gods?

266
00:17:31,180 --> 00:17:32,010
Pharaoh,

267
00:17:32,100 --> 00:17:35,377
I'm sure you and the former king
have a lot of catching up to do,

268
00:17:35,460 --> 00:17:37,757
but we are in the middle
of something here.

269
00:17:37,840 --> 00:17:40,193
And you interrupted me at the best part,

270
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:43,497
just as my Dearbound was about
to deliver the finishing blow,

271
00:17:43,580 --> 00:17:45,227
forcing you into submission!

272
00:17:45,580 --> 00:17:46,410
Now,

273
00:17:46,493 --> 00:17:48,377
any last words before
I end this shadow game

274
00:17:48,460 --> 00:17:50,989
and seize control of
your Millennium Items?

275
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:52,830
Good.

276
00:17:52,913 --> 00:17:54,361
Then, Deerbaum, bring me victory.

277
00:17:54,580 --> 00:17:56,080
Stop right there, Bakura.

278
00:17:56,640 --> 00:17:57,470
Ha!

279
00:17:57,553 --> 00:17:58,495
Too little, too late.

280
00:17:58,620 --> 00:17:59,600
Finish him off.

281
00:17:59,980 --> 00:18:00,820
Hold on.

282
00:18:01,100 --> 00:18:03,457
There's something you
seem to have forgotten.

283
00:18:03,540 --> 00:18:05,280
Allow me to remind you.

284
00:18:05,620 --> 00:18:07,900
I can call the Egyptian gods.

285
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:09,340
What does he mean?

286
00:18:09,560 --> 00:18:12,040
Could it be the legendary god monsters?

287
00:18:12,520 --> 00:18:16,397
Are you referring to the three Egyptian
gods that guard the pharaoh's tomb?

288
00:18:16,480 --> 00:18:18,917
The scriptures state
that only the chosen king

289
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:21,824
will know the names of
these legendary monsters.

290
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:27,240
But wait, does this mean you are
the chosen king in the prophecy?

291
00:18:28,180 --> 00:18:31,260
Legendary gods of Egypt,
please hear my call.

292
00:18:31,620 --> 00:18:35,920
In the name of every pharaoh that
came before, I now beseech thee.

293
00:18:36,700 --> 00:18:41,940
Awaken, mighty Ovalis, and rid the
sacred palace of this darkness.

294
00:18:53,700 --> 00:18:57,400
I summon Obelisk the Tormentor!

295
00:19:02,720 --> 00:19:04,920
This can't be happening!

296
00:19:05,540 --> 00:19:06,940
Obelisk the Tormentor!

297
00:19:07,800 --> 00:19:10,220
Attack Fist of Fury!

298
00:19:11,940 --> 00:19:15,700
Now, Diabau, use the power of Blue Eyes!

299
00:19:15,940 --> 00:19:17,380
White lightning attack!

300
00:19:36,280 --> 00:19:38,980
I could swear I just heard Blue Eyes.
